WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.245
Lesson 3.3.

00:00:02.245 --> 00:00:04.250
Liquidations and cascades.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.291
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:06.291 --> 00:00:08.828
able to know exactly what a liquidation costs

00:00:08.828 --> 00:00:11.035
you, and how to avoid ever reaching one.

00:00:12.335 --> 00:00:13.625
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:15.310
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.025
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.025 --> 00:00:19.550
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.712
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:26.427
When HF drops below 1, a liquidator (usually

00:00:26.427 --> 00:00:29.158
a bot) repays part of your debt (up

00:00:29.158 --> 00:00:32.345
to the close factor, often 50%) and takes

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:35.608
that value of your collateral plus a bonus

00:00:35.608 --> 00:00:38.867
(the liquidation penalty, often 5–10%).

00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:42.764
Liquidations sell collateral into a falling market, which can

00:00:42.764 --> 00:00:46.472
push prices lower and trigger more liquidations: a cascade.

00:00:47.772 --> 00:00:50.287
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:00:50.287 --> 00:00:52.662
Your position from 3.2.

00:00:52.662 --> 00:00:56.878
ETH falls to $1,490, health factor just under 1:

00:00:56.878 --> 00:01:01.869
Defence ladder: health factor 2.0 to alert; health factor

00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:06.344
1.7 to repay from reserve or add collateral; health

00:01:06.344 --> 00:01:11.032
factor 1.5 to sell part of the collateral yourself.

00:01:11.032 --> 00:01:13.112
Never wait for 1.1.

00:01:13.112 --> 00:01:19.425
A liquidator repays $6,000 (50% close factor)

00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:24.640
and seizes $6,000 times 1.05 = $6,300

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.096
of ETH about 4.228 ETH.

00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:31.020
The $300 bonus is a pure loss to you,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.021
on top of having sold ETH near the low.

00:01:35.321 --> 00:01:36.781
Here's your checklist.

00:01:36.781 --> 00:01:38.316
Do it now, for real.

00:01:38.316 --> 00:01:42.101
First, Defence ladder written with exact HF levels.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:46.251
Next, Reserve set aside to repay (Module 12.4).

00:01:46.251 --> 00:01:50.586
And finally, Oracle for my collateral known (Module 5.3).

00:01:51.886 --> 00:01:53.096
Question 1.

00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:54.631
What does a liquidator receive?

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:01.330
The answer: Collateral equal to the

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.546
debt repaid plus a bonus (penalty).

00:02:04.846 --> 00:02:06.091
Question 2.

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:09.116
Why is self-deleveraging better than being liquidated?

00:02:13.536 --> 00:02:15.461
The answer: You avoid the penalty

00:02:15.461 --> 00:02:17.216
and choose the size and timing.

00:02:18.516 --> 00:02:19.786
Question 3.

00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:21.191
How do cascades form?

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:30.200
The answer: Liquidations sell collateral, pushing prices down,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.041
which pushes more positions below HF 1.

00:02:34.341 --> 00:02:36.856
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:40.846
Next up, Lesson 3.4: Borrowing strategies & looping.
